{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Despised</b> — linked in his eyes even to the abhorrent. The meaning: for one who serves HaShem, every commandment he observed and every good he did is despised and contemptible in his eyes, compared to what he is obligated to do for the honor of his Creator. And such is the way of the righteous, that they seek to ascend to a level holier and more honored than their own. And he said: 'he honors,' opposite 'despised.'" "<b>Sworn to harm</b> — himself, as it were, like fasting, for he denies the flesh."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:18.829706504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}